  "title": "Schneller als …",
  "subtitle": "The comparative, so … wie and als",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "type": "overview",
      "label": "Überblick",
      "title": "Lesson intro",
      "minutes": 40,
      "learn": [
        "The comparative is the adjective plus -er. Many short adjectives take an umlaut: alt → älter, stark → stärker.",
        "Irregular: gut → besser, viel → mehr, gern → lieber. hoch → höher, groß → größer, teuer → teurer.",
        "Equality is (genau)so … wie. Inequality is the comparative plus als.",
        "In front of a noun the comparative still takes an adjective ending: der stärkere Schmerz."
      ],
      "vocab": [
        {
          "de": "Schmerz",
          "article": "der",
          "plural": "die Schmerzen",
          "en": "pain",
          "emoji": "⚡",
          "glossaryKey": "schmerz"
        },
        {
          "de": "Blutdruck",
          "article": "der",
          "plural": "Blutdruck",
          "en": "blood pressure",
          "emoji": "❤️",
          "glossaryKey": "blutdruck"
        },
        {
          "de": "Wasser",
